  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"751\" data-end=\"854\">\n<p data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"854\"><strong data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"765\">Negative</strong>: No significant IgE antibodies to Metronidazole detected; IgE-mediated allergy unlikely.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"972\">\n<p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"972\"><strong data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"869\">Positive</strong>: Indicates sensitization; Metronidazole may cause allergic reactions (e.g., rash, hives, anaphylaxis).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"972\"><strong data-start=\"976\" data-end=\"984\">Note</strong>: Some Metronidazole reactions are non-IgE-mediated (delayed type), so clinical history is crucial even if IgE is negative</p>",
